%I A400185 #29 Sep 22 2026 22:09:09
%S A400185 0,1,2,3,3,5,5,7,7,8,10,10,11,13,13,14,15,17,17,18,17,21,21,22,21
%N A400185 An analog of A399633 for buildings on a square spiral on an infinite chessboard.
%C A400185 We are constructing buildings along the square spiral with its cells numbered starting at 0, as in A308884 and A274641.
%C A400185 An important difference from A399633 is that here each building must fill its square plot. That is, the cross-section of a building is a square that exactly equals the square that it sits on. A building of height h is a 1 X 1 X h column.
%C A400185 A building can see another if there is a clear line of sight from a point on the top of one building to a point on the top of the other building.
%C A400185 Then a(n) is the smallest number h for which it is true to say that the building on square n can see exactly h earlier buildings. If no such h exists, the sequence ends.
%C A400185 Note that the squares are indexed starting at 0 (in contrast to A399633).
%H A400185 N. J. A. Sloane, <a href="/A400185/a400185.jpg">Illustration of a(0)-a(24).</a>
%e A400185 The spiral begins:
%e A400185 .
%e A400185 .......................
%e A400185 .16--15--14--13--12..29.
%e A400185 ..|...............|...|.
%e A400185 .17...4---3---2..11..28.
%e A400185 ..|...|...|...|...|...|.
%e A400185 .18...5...0---1..10..27.
%e A400185 ..|...|...|...|...|...|.
%e A400185 .19...6---7---8---9..26.
%e A400185 ..|...|...|...|.......|.
%e A400185 .20--21--22--23--24--25.
%e A400185 .
%e A400185 After a(0)=0, a(1)=1, a(2)=2, a(3)=3, a building of height 4 in square 4 would be able to see all four earlier buildings, but a building of height 3 could only see three earlier building (its view of the height-2 building being totally blocked by first height-3 building). Since 3<4, we must take a(4) = 3.
%e A400185 a(8)=8 because a building of height 8 at square 8 can see 8 of the previous buildings (all, that is, except the second building of height 5), while no smaller value of h works.
%Y A400185 Cf. A399633.
%Y A400185 See also A308884 and A274641
%K A400185 nonn,tabf,more,new
%O A400185 0,3
